---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import wallpapers from '../data/wallpapers.json';
---

<Layout title="Photo credits" pageTitle="Photo credits" kind="page">
  <article class="page-content credits-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Behind the desktop</p>
    <h1>Photo credits</h1>
    <p class="lead">Real places. Real photographs. A few things I like, brought together on a quiet desktop.</p>
    <p>Sources and photographers are credited below. The Porsche and Theatro images use resized WebP variants; the other photographs retain their source JPEGs. The F1 photographs use grayscale and viewport-filling cropping only. Porsche and Theatro also use darkening and optional gentle pan and zoom.</p>
    <p>Creative Commons photographs retain their individually listed licenses. No generative editing or compositing was used. Motion comes from still photographs, not video footage.</p>

    <div class="entry-list credits-list">
      {wallpapers.map((wallpaper) => (
        <section class="entry" id={wallpaper.id} aria-labelledby={`credit-${wallpaper.id}`}>
          <img src={wallpaper.src} alt={wallpaper.title} width="320" height="213" loading="lazy" />
          <div class="credit-details"><p class="eyebrow">Photography · {wallpaper.license}</p>
          <h2 id={`credit-${wallpaper.id}`}>{wallpaper.title}</h2>
          <p>{wallpaper.credit}</p>
          <p>
            <a class="text-link" href={wallpaper.source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original photograph and source</a>
            {wallpaper.licenseUrl && <>{' · '}<a class="text-link" href={wallpaper.licenseUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{wallpaper.license} license</a></>}
          </p>
          {wallpaper.licenseUrl && <p>
            <a class="text-link" href={wallpaper.src} download>Download desktop adaptation</a>
            {' · '}
            <a class="text-link" href={wallpaper.mobileSrc} download>Download mobile adaptation</a>
          </p>}
        </div></section>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p>Photographers, licensors, brands, teams, venues, and other rights holders do not sponsor or endorse this site. The photo licenses do not grant trademark, privacy, or publicity rights. The Eau Rouge photograph is historical; the Hamilton Ferrari photograph depicts the 2026 SF-26.</p>
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/">Back home</a></p>
  </article>
</Layout>
